QUESTION=Identify the quoted work/author and explain what the epigraph is doing here.
RESULT=The epigraph is from James Thomson's The Castle of Indolence (1748), Canto I stanza VI. Irving uses its drowsy, dreamlike imagery to establish Sleepy Hollow's atmosphere before the narrative begins; secondary literary commentary also identifies thematic relevance beyond scene-setting.
